QuestGuidance.Register("en",372,{
[11873]="700544A4\n1\tComplete quests in the Circle of Sorrow (total: 10)\tYou should complete quests in the Circle of Sorrow in Minas Morgul.\n2\tTalk to Damrod in Barad Orhant\tDamrod can be found in Barad Orhant in Minas Morgul. You should talk to Damrod.\n3\tComplete 'Instance: Into the Circle of Madness'\030Enter Barad Elenath, the Star-gazers' Spire\tThe entrance to Barad Elenath can be found in the Circle of Sorrow. You should enter the tower of Barad Elenath.\n4\tTalk to Rhadrog in Barad Elenath\tRhadrog can be found in Barad Elenath in Minas Morgul. You should talk to Rhadrog.\n",
[11874]="700544AA\n1\tComplete quests in the Circle of Wrath (total: 10)\tThe Circle of Wrath is the lowest of the levels of Minas Morgul. You should complete quests in the Circle of Wrath.\n2\tTalk to Damrod in Barad Angarth\tDamrod can be found at the tower of Barad Angarth. You should talk to Damrod.\n3\tComplete 'Instance: Into the Circle of Sorrow'\030Enter Barad Orhant, the Tower of the Treegarth\tThe entrance to Barad Orhant can be found in the Circle of Wrath. You should enter the tower of Barad Orhant.\n4\tTalk to Damrod in Barad Orhant\tDamrod can be found in Barad Orhant. You should talk to Damrod.\n",
[11875]="7000F029\n1\tTalk to Lothrandir\tMake your way far to the east and north to Sûri-kylä, the City in the Ice.\n",
[11876]="70040DF7\n1\tFind the wharf\tThe wharf is on the eastern side of Dol Amroth. You should make your way to the wharf.\n2\tSpeak with Anírwen\tAnírwen is at the wharf on the east side of Dol Amroth. You should speak with Anírwen.\n3\tFind the Artisan's Quarter\tThe Artisan's Quarter is in north Dol Amroth. You should make your way to the Artisan's Quarter.\n4\tSpeak with someone in the Artisan's Quarter\tThe Artisan's Quarter is in north-east Dol Amroth. You should speak with someone at the Artisan's Quarter.\n5\tFind the Keep of the Swan-knights\tThe Keep of the Swan-knights is in north Dol Amroth. You should make your way to the Keep of the Swan-knights.\n6\tSpeak with a swan-knight\tThe Keep of the Swan-knights is in north Dol Amroth. You should speak with one of the swan-knights.\n7\tFind Inzibel's Walk\tInzibel's Walk is in north-east Dol Amroth. You should make your way to Inzibel's Walk.\n8\tFind the Court of the Fount\tThe Court of the Fount is in the centre of Dol Amroth. You should make your way to the Court of the Fount.\n9\tSpeak with someone in the Court of the Fount\tThe Court of the Fount is in the centre of Dol Amroth. You should speak with someone at the Court of the Fount.\n10\tFind the Library of Saphadzîr\tThe Library of Saphadzîr is just south of the centre of Dol Amroth. You should make your way to the Library of Saphadzîr.\n11\tFind the Scholar's Quarter\tThe Scholar's Quarter is in southern Dol Amroth. You should make your way to the Scholar's Quarter.\n12\tSpeak with someone in the Scholar's Quarter\tThe Scholar's Quarter is in southern Dol Amroth. You should speak with someone in the Scholar's Quarter.\n13\tFind the Mason's Court\tThe Mason's Court is in southern Dol Amroth. You should make your way to the Mason's Court.\n14\tSpeak with Laegened\tLaegened, the master stone-mason, can be found in the Mason's Court. You should speak with Laegened.\n15\tFind the Harper's Court\tThe Harper's Court is in western Dol Amroth. You should make your way to the Harper's Court.\n16\tSpeak with someone in the Harper's Court\tThe Harper's Court is in western Dol Amroth. You should speak with someone in the Harper's Court.\n17\tSpeak with Lothíriel\tLothíriel is in the Great Hall of the Prince. You should speak with Lothíriel.\n",
[11877]="70009792\n1\tTalk to Aragorn in Rivendell\tAragorn is in one of the guest rooms of Elrond's House. Master Elrond told you of Aragorn's youth and agreed that Narsil must be reforged. He has decided on a name for the new sword: Andúril, Flame of the West.\n",
[11878]="70071E8F\n1\tSpeak with Quartermaster Alahamâr at Zajâna\tThe leaders of Zajâna are not as welcoming as others may be. Too many times has an open hand quickly turned to a shackle. Valakhâri directed you to introduce yourself to the Alahamâr for further instruction.\n2\tSpeak with Valakhâri in Zajâna\tYour introduction to the quartermaster is complete. Return to Valakhâri and tell her you are ready to assist the city and her people.\n",
[11879]="70067EDA\n1\tLeave Driftwood alone with his thoughts\tDriftwood asked you to give him some time to think in peace.\n2\tTalk to Driftwood somewhere outside the city\tDriftwood has likely wandered the surrounds outside the city. You should look for him and see how he is feeling.\n",
[11880]="70067651\n1\tStand by the lone tree to the south-east, by the farms, and blow the whistle\tThe fruit trees far to the south-east, by the farms outside the city, are of interest to Gwallang the Limlinn.\n2\tTalk to Gwallang by the tree he likes\tGwallang has arrived and hops around excitedly on a rock by the tree.\n3\tCollect a fistful of grass and hay from the haystack to the north-east\tThe haystack to the north-east might provide the materials Gwallang will need to construct his nest.\n4\tHelp Gwallang construct his ideal nest\tGwallang's potential nesting place is by the lone tree to the south-west of the haystack.\n5\tTalk to Gwallang by his new nest\tGwallang seems very pleased with his new nest.\n",
[11881]="70067532\n1\tGimli asked you to speak with nearby dock-workers about the Kindred of the Coins.\t\n2\tTalk to dock-workers in the Sail-haven about the Kindred of the Coins\tGimli asked you to speak with nearby dock-workers about the Kindred of the Coins.\n3\tTalk to dock-workers in the Sail-haven about the Kindred of the Coins\tGimli asked you to speak with nearby dock-workers about the Kindred of the Coins.\n4\tTalk to Legolas in the Sail-haven\tLegolas stands in an alley in the Sail-haven.\n5\tFind the office of the Harbour Warden in the tall blue tower\tThe office of the harbour warden is in the tall blue tower out in the water south of the Sail-haven.\n6\tTalk to Eshmun's assistant outside the tall blue tower south of the Sail-haven\tThe Harbour Warden's assistant is outside the tall blue tower located in the water south of the Sail-haven.\n7\tTalk to Gimli across the bridge in the Sail-haven\030Talk to Legolas across the bridge in the Sail-haven\tGimli and Legolas stand across the bridge from the Harbour Warden's tower.\n",
[11882]="70067650\n1\tPost notices for Galengam's market stall (0/3)\tGalengam has asked you to put up notices for his new stall to the south, within the Sail-haven.\n2\tPost the notices for Galengam's market stall (1/3)\tGalengam has asked you to put up notices for his new stall to the south, within the Sail-haven.\n3\tPost the notices for Galengam's market stall (2/3)\tGalengam has asked you to put up notices for his new stall to the south, within the Sail-haven.\n4\tTalk to the richly-dressed man staring at the notice you just posted\tA richly-dressed man has commented on the notice you just posted.\n5\tWait for Azagath to leave\tThat man was Azagath Sea-shadow, the leader of the Kindred of the Coins!\n6\tLook for Cruel Dancer in the vicinity of Galengam's market stall\tAzagath said he would visit Galengam's market stall to the north. Is Cruel Dancer nearby? If she kills her target now, you might never see Thorongil again!\n7\tTalk to Galengam at his market stall\tGalengam's market stall is to the north, in the Sail-haven.\n8\tTalk to Azagath Sea-shadow at Galengam's market stall\tGalengam's market stall is to the north, in the Sail-haven.\n9\tWait for Azagath to leave\tAzagath Sea-shadow moves away and is lost in the crowd.\n10\tTalk to Galengam at his market stall\tGalengam's market stall is in the Sail-haven.\n",
[11883]="70067652\n1\tWait to see what happens\tGangur Farwend is feeling frustrated.\n2\tTalk to Carver Gírma outside the Shoreward Stone\tCarver Gírma has called for your attention.\n3\tFind the Old Bastion Inn to the south-west of the Shoreward Stone, in the Fleet-fast\tCarver Gírma offered to speak with you and Gangur Farwend at the Old Bastion Inn to the south-west, in the Fleet-fast.\n4\tTalk to Gangur Farwend at the Old Bastion Inn\tGangur Farwend is eager to speak with Carver Gírma at the Old Bastion Inn.\n5\tTalk to Carver Gírma at the Old Bastion Inn\tCarver Gírma is at the Old Bastion Inn.\n6\tTalk to Gangur Farwend at the Old Bastion Inn\tGangur Farwend is at the Old Bastion Inn.\n",
[11884]="70067531\n1\tListen for mention of Khâsha to the north, outside the Black Anchor Tavern in the Lower Ward\tSigileth wanted you to listen for mention of Khâsha to the north, outside the Black Anchor Tavern in the Lower Ward.\n2\tListen for mention of Khâsha further north, outside the Cat's Grin Tavern in the Lower Ward\tSigileth wanted you to listen for mention of Khâsha further north, outside the Cat's Grin Tavern in the Lower Ward.\n3\tTalk to the Lower Ward resident outside the Cat's Grin Tavern about Khâsha\tYou think you have overheard the name \"Khâsha\" and should ask the Lower Ward resident for more information.\n4\tFind the Khâsha who lives in the Lower Ward\tSomeone named Khâsha lives to the north-east, in the Lower Ward.\n5\tTalk to Khâsha in the Lower Ward\tKhâsha lives in the Lower Ward, north-east of the Cat's Grin Tavern.\n6\tTalk to Sigileth in the Lower Ward\tSigileth is helping you investigate the mystery of Khâsha in the Lower Ward.\n7\tFind Phêlex outside the Guild Hall in the Lower Ward\tYou were told you might find Phêlex near the Guild Hall in the Lower Ward.\n8\tTalk to Phêlex by the Guild Hall in the Lower Ward\tPhêlex is by the Guild Hall in the Lower Ward.\n9\tTalk to Sigileth by the Guild Hall in the Lower Ward\tSigileth has come with you to meet with Phêlex in the Lower Ward.\n",
[11885]="70067530\n1\tSirgon has asked you to speak to residents of the Upper Ward so you may learn where Belondor now lives.\t\n2\tTalk to residents of the Upper Ward and learn where Belondor lives\tSirgon has asked you to speak to residents of the Upper Ward so you may learn where Belondor now lives.\n3\tTalk to Mêshka at one of the markets in the Upper Ward or in the Sail-haven\tYou learned that Belondor's wife Mêshka was recently spotted on her way south, perhaps to one of the markets of the Upper Ward or in the Sail-haven.\n4\tWait for Sirgon to arrive\tYou learned that Belondor's wife Mêshka was recently spotted on her way to one of the markets in the Upper Ward or the Sail-haven.\n5\tTalk to Mêshka at one of the markets in the Upper Ward or the Sail-haven\tMêshka stares at Sirgon coldly.\n6\tWait for Mêshka to leave\tMêshka hurries away.\n7\tMeet with Mêshka at her home in the Upper Ward\tMêshka and Belondor live to the north-east, in the Upper Ward.\n8\tTalk to Mêshka at her home in the Upper Ward\tMêshka and Belondor live in the north-eastern reaches of the Upper Ward.\n9\tTalk to Sirgon outside Mêshka's home in the Upper Ward\tSirgon seems to ignore the nearby guards, and keep his eyes on Mêshka.\n10\tTalk to Mêshka at her home in the Upper Ward\tMêshka and Belondor live in the north-eastern reaches of the Upper Ward.\n11\tWait for Mêshka to leave\tMêshka and Belondor live in the north-eastern reaches of the Upper Ward.\n12\tTalk to Sirgon outside Mêshka's home in the Upper Ward\tSirgon stands outside the home of Mêshka and Belondor in the Upper Ward.\n13\tTalk to Sirgon to the south-west, outside the Upper Ward\tSirgon has been banished from the Upper Ward. You should speak with him to the south-west, in the Sail-haven.\n",
[11886]="7006750C\n1\tLinger by the clay jar to the south-west, in the Fleet-fast\tNauriel asked you to linger by the clay jar to the south-west so you can observe the movement of guards within the Fleet-fast.\n2\tObserve the movement of guards within the Fleet-fast\tNauriel asked you to linger by a clay jar so you can observe the movement of guards within the Fleet-fast.\n3\tLinger by a clay jar further to the west\tNauriel asked you to linger at a clay jar further to the west so you can observe the movement of guards within the Fleet-fast.\n4\tObserve the movement of guards within the Fleet-fast\tNauriel asked you to linger by a clay jar so you can observe the movement of guards within the Fleet-fast.\n5\tLinger by the clay jar further to the west\tNauriel asked you to linger by a clay jar further to the west so you can observe the movement of guards within the Fleet-fast.\n6\tTalk to the Fleet-fast guard\tA suspicious guard of the Fleet-fast has called you over to him.\n7\tTalk to Nauriel to the north-east, outside the Fleet-fast\tNauriel waits for your report where you left her, to the north-east outside the Fleet-fast.\n",
[11887]="70067533\n1\tTalk to the Guard of the Gaol in the Fleet-fast\tA guard stands watch outside the gaol in the Fleet-fast.\n2\tTalk to Daxamat outside the gaol in the Fleet-fast\tDaxamat stands outside the gaol in the Fleet-fast.\n3\tExamine the arena match-ups in the Tor-gardens\tThe various match-ups for the arena can be found in the Tor-gardens.\n4\tYou should see how bad things may be for Itûr by speaking to people familiar with the arena in the Tor-gardens.\t\n5\tTalk to Daxamat outside the arena in the Tor-gardens\tDaxamat is outside the arena in the Tor-gardens, considering his friend's likely fate if he faces Rothog the Storm in battle.\n6\tGive Daxamat's money-purse to the Guard of the Gaol in the Fleet-fast\tOnly the guard outside the gaol in the Fleet-fast can save Itûr now.\n7\tWait for the guard to come back outside\tThe Guard of the Gaol has gone inside to speak with Itûr.\n8\tWait for the guard to come back outside\tThe Guard of the Gaol has gone inside to speak with Itûr.\n9\tTalk to the Guard of the Gaol in the Fleet-fast\tThe guard of the gaol has finally come back outside.\n10\tTalk to Daxamat outside the gaol in the Fleet-fast\tDaxamat stands outside the gaol in the Fleet-fast.\n",
[11888]="70067653\n1\tAppraise the barracks in the Fleet-fast\030Appraise the western side of the Fleet-fast bridge\030Appraise the eastern side of the Fleet-fast bridge\tBruidis has asked you to appraise the defences of the barracks, and the eastern and western ends of the bridge that spans the Fleet-fast.\n2\tTalk to Bruidis by the south-eastern gate in the Fleet-fast\tBruidis is located by the south-eastern gate in the Fleet-fast.\n3\tTalk to Rossaran in the Lower Ward\tRossaran is to the north of the Fleet-fast, in the Lower Ward.\n",
[11889]="70067C52\n1\tMeet up with Driftwood in the Tor-gardens\tDriftwood has asked to you meet you in the Tor-gardens.\n2\tTalk to Driftwood outside the arena in the Tor-gardens\tDriftwood is by the arena in the Tor-gardens.\n3\tDriftwood asked you to speak with visitors to the Tor-gardens about what the future might hold for such a man as he.\t\n4\tTalk to Driftwood in the Tor-gardens\tDriftwood is by the arena in the Tor-gardens.\n",
[11890]="7006764F\n1\tTalk to Elladan at the White Gate on the eastern side of the Lower Ward\tElladan is by the White Gate on the eastern side of the Lower Ward.\n2\tTalk to Elrohir by one of the farms to the east, outside the city\tElladan and Elrohir have decided to investigate the man's information, meeting him beside one of the farms outside the city. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n3\tTalk to Elrohir outside the White Gate on the eastern side of the Lower Ward\030Talk to Elladan outside the White Gate on the eastern side of the Lower Ward\tElladan and Elrohir agreed to meet you back outside the White Gate on the eastern side of the Lower Ward of the city.\n",
[11891]="70061F09\n1\tCollect severed Orc ears (total: 10)\tMayor Cadwallon Nevit has asked you to defeat Orcs among the ruins of Tharbad. Tharbad is located in south-west Cardolan.\n2\tBring the ears to Mayor Nevit\tYou should bring the severed Orc ears to Mayor Cadwallon Nevit. Mayor Nevit has returned to Herne, in central Cardolan.\n",
[11892]="70028C9A\n1\tTalk to Garrun in the Isendale\tGarrun is encamped against a cliff face far to the west of Forthbrond, north of Cuvnerth. Ardwyn has asked you to seek out the scout Garrun at the western edge of the Isendale and lend him your aid.\n",
[11893]="70048C84\n1\tComplete: One Really Long Rope\tStrong vines can be found in the trees near Seregost. You should cobble together a rope from the vines.\n2\tComplete: The Secrets of Seregost\tViznak can be found near Seregost in eastern Agarnaith. You should talk to Viznak and complete your mission in Seregost.\n3\tTalk to Rhadrog\tRhadrog can be found in Viznak's hideout. You should talk to Rhadrog.\n",
[11894]="70018F17\n1\tEnter the maze\tThe entrance to the hedge maze is near the festival grounds in the Horse-fields, a distance to the north of Bree-town. Gil Plover has challenged you to get through the maze, from start to finish, before the time runs out.\n2\tFind your way out before the time expires\tThe exit to the hedge-maze is around here somewhere...or is it? You should try to find your way out of the maze before the time runs out. Gil Plover got out in no time at all compared to the amount you've been given. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n3\tTalk to Gil Plover outside the maze in the Horse-fields\tGil Plover is standing near the hedge maze, which is very near the festival grounds of Bree-land, north of Bree-town. You should speak with Gil Plover, for you can prove that you were able to best his challenge that you would not get through the maze in admirable time.\n",
[11895]="70022745\n1\tDestroy gwiber egg-clutches (total: 3)\tGwiber-nests may be found to the south of Zudrugund. Frithgeir has asked you to hunt down nests of gwiber-eggs and destroy them.\n2\tTalk to Frithgeir at Zudrugund\tFrithgeir is at Zudrugund, north of the gwiber-nests. You should return to Frithgeir and inform him that you have destroyed many gwiber-eggs.\n",
[11896]="7002D550\n1\tThe strange light came from the far end of the Old Silvertine City from where Öndótt stands. You should find the source of the strange light.\t\n2\tBring the crystals to Öndótt\tÖndótt is at the top of the stair in the Old Silvertine City. You should return to Öndótt with the crystals you gathered.\n",
[11897]="7002F9A2\n1\tSpeak to Norbald at Enswith's farm, north of the mead hall\tNorbald can be found at the north-west edge of Endwith's farm, north-east of the mead hall. Norbald has gone to scout the enemy forces at the perimeter of Enswith's farm.\n2\tDefeat Uruk-hai Raiders (total: 4)\030Defeat Uruk-hai Skirmishers (total: 2)\tThe enemy Uruk-hai can be found west of Norbald's location, north of the mead hall. Norbald has asked for your help in repelling the mounted Uruk-hai approaching Faldham.\n3\tSpeak to Norbald at Enswith's farm\tNorbald awaits at the north-west part of Enswith's farm. Norbald needs to know that you have repelled several of the mounted Orcs approaching Faldham.\n",
[11898]="700350F2\n1\tTell Thane Cynegar of Scylfig that battle looms near\tThane Cynegar resides in the town of Scylfig in the northern Writhendowns. You should speak with Thane Cynegar in the Mead Hall of Scylfig to warn him of the looming attack.\n",
[11899]="70072F03\n1\tExamine the parchments outside the central keep of Starkhaven\tParchments spread upon a table outside the central keep of Starkhaven describe the dangerous authority of Ghómbok Bóro.\n2\tAppraise the danger posed by the opening of the Weirway Gate\030Find the walkway near the Weirway Gate, located behind the central keep of Starkhaven\tYou should find the Weirway Gate behind the central keep of Starkhaven and appraise the danger if it is opened.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have appraised the danger posed by the opening of the Weirway Gate, and found it to be substantial.\n4\tThe man possessing Ghómbok Bóro's command lives to the south-east of the Weirway Gate, not far from the courtyard displaying an impressive lion statue.\t\n5\tBurn Ghómbok Bóro's command in a nearby brazier\tThe command to open the Weirway Gate is too dangerous. You should burn it in a nearby brazier.\n6\tCompleted\tYou have saved the residents of Adagím from Ghómbok Bóro's command... at least for now.\n",
[11900]="70058741\n1\tFind and defeat Commander Mozgúth\tCommander Mozgúth can be found at Zudramdân. You should find and defeat Commander Mozgúth.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have successfully defeated Commander Mozgúth.\n",
[11901]="70060012\n1\tTravel to Eiricháv\tEiricháv can be found in north west Câr Bronach. You should travel to Eiricháv.\n2\tTalk to Uzvát outside Eiricháv\tEiricháv can be found in north west Câr Bronach. You should talk to Uzvát outside Eiricháv.\n3\tEnter Eiricháv\tEiricháv can be found in north west Câr Bronach. You should enter Eiricháv.\n4\tTalk to Soltakh of the Trév Gállorg in Eiricháv\tEiricháv can be found in north west Câr Bronach. You should talk to Soltakh of the Trév Gállorg in Eiricháv.\n5\tComplete: 'Roots of the Land' with Aighrig\030Complete: 'Thwarting the Iron Pass' with Suilgál\030Complete: 'A Warning to Tâg Fógarrach' with Monathár\030Complete: 'Cave Growth' with Fuisach\tEiricháv can be found in north west Câr Bronach. You should complete quests for the hillmen in Eiricháv.\n6\tTalk to Soltakh of the Trév Gállorg in Eiricháv\tEiricháv can be found in north west Câr Bronach. You should talk to Soltakh of the Trév Gállorg in Eiricháv.\n",
[11902]="7004A81A\n1\tDefeat foes in Dor Amarth (total: 20)\tIngold has asked you to defeat foes in Dor Amarth.\n",
[11903]="7004A81E\n1\tDefeat foes in Talath Úrui (total: 20)\tBregdal has asked you to defeat foes in Talath Úrui.\n",
[11904]="700162B9\n1\tExplore the cooling chamber with Slagvi\tSlagvi is at the Dolven-view camp. Slagvi wishes to enter the Cooling Chamber in hopes to restore the Great Delving's natural water system to an operational state.\n2\tTalk to Slagvi at the Dolven-view camp\tSlagvi is at the Dolven-view camp. You should speak with Slagvi.\n",
})
